earance settings\nL113: You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL114: \nL115:   1. cite61†flashinfer-ai L116:   2. cite62†flashinfer L117: ## Repository navigation\nL118: \nL119:   *   * cite62†Code L120:   * cite63†Issues423 (423) L121:   * cite64†Pull requests846 (846) L122:   * cite65†Discussions L123:   * cite66†Actions L124:   * cite67†Projects L125:   * cite68†Security and quality L126:   * cite69†Insights L127: \nL128: More items\nL129: # [CAKE] Long-term CAKE-generated Kernel Progress Tracker #4254\nL130: \nL131: New issue\nL132: \nL133: Copy link\nL134: \nL135: New issue\nL136: \nL137: Copy link\nL138: \nL139: Open\nL140: \nL141: cite70†Task L142: \nL143: 25 / 45 25 of 45 issues completed\nL144: \nL145: Open\nL146: \nL147: cite71†[CAKE] Long-term CAKE-generated Kernel Progress Tracker #4254\nL148: \nL149: Task\nL150: \nL151: 25 / 45 25 of 45 issues completed\nL152: \nL153: Copy link\nL154: \nL155: Assignees\nL156: \nL157: Labels\nL158: cite72†needs-triage cite73†op: linear attentionKDA, mamba, GDN, etc. review filtering. KDA, mamba, GDN, etc. review filtering.cite74†op: miscnorm, activation, sampling, RoPE, quantization, etc. norm, activation, sampling, RoPE, quantization, etc.\nL159: ## Description\nL160: \nL161: cite75†yyihuang L162: \nL163: opened cite76†on Jul 29, 2026 L164: \nL165: Issue body actions\nL166: \nL167: To track multi-platform kernels generated from CAKE 🍰 harness + claude/codex agent.\nL168: \nL169: We are more than happy to take any new kernel challenges!\nL170: \nL171: Feel free to reach out/leave your comments/create sub-issues here to submit your customized CAKE kernel request. And we will bake it for you!\nL172: We know many of you have been asking for training kernels—and we heard you. You have had your CAKE going forward; now it is time to take it back! Follow the dedicated forward & backward tracker at cite77†#4642 , bring us your toughest training bottleneck, and let us bake the full pass together. 🍰🔥\nL173: \nL174: And we recommend using agent to index the kernels you need. 😜\nL175: ## Kernel categories\nL176: \nL177: Pull requests are tracked in the category sub-issues below, with detailed sections and links to each PR. Please add new PRs to the corresponding category.\nL178: ### Communication\nL179: \nL180: Sub-issue: cite78†#6593 L181: \nL182: MoE all-reduce/finalize and residual-add/RMSNorm/combine fusion; MNNVL, Ulysses and DCP all-to-all; all-gather matmul and sequence parallelism; QKV/Norm/RoPE and MiniMax ICP exchange; FP8 GEMM + all-reduce; NVFP4-transport TP all-reduce with residual + RMSNorm fusion; Kimi-K3 TP12 tails, SM120 PCIe communication and MoK.\nL183: ### Attention\nL184: \nL185: Sub-issue: cite79†#6594 L186: \nL187: FMHA variants (paged/DCP/GQA, MiniMax sparse, NVFP4, Sage/VSA, and MiniMax-H3 dense/packed-varlen); MLA K concatenation, decode and sparse MLA, including DSA forward/backward. Also covers fused pre-attention/output projection, QKV quantize-and-pack, QK RMSNorm/RoPE/KV append, Kimi-K3 AttnRes, and DSA indexer logits/top-k.\nL188: ### Linear Attention & State Space\nL189: \nL190: Sub-issue: cite80†#6595 L191: \nL192: Recurrent KDA prefill, decode and training; Gated Delta Rule context-parallel and non-CP prefill, FP32-state paths and the source-only Blackwell backend; Mamba SSDCombined and selective state update.\nL193: ### GEMM / BMM\nL194: \nL195: Sub-issue: cite81†#6596 L196: \nL197: BF16 BMM, BF16 x FP4/NVFP4/FP8 and grouped GEMM, DeepGEMM/TinyGEMM2, all-gather matmul and router GEMM. Includes SVDQuant, runtime BF16 LoRA, per-token quantize + GEMM, projection gradients, MiniMax-H3 FC1 + SwiGLU/full-MLP fusion, and Kimi-K3 FP8 projection.\nL198: \nL199: ### MoE & Routing\nL200: \nL201: Sub-issue: cite82†#6597 L202: \nL203: Fused MoE, AlphaMoE, MegaMoE and BGMV MoE; DeepSeek fused routing; Kimi-K3 Stable LatentMoE and fused router; warp-decode kernels.\nL204: ### Activation & Quantization\nL205: \nL206: Sub-issue: cite83†#6598 L207: \nL208: MXFP8 quantization, fused SwiGLU + MXFP8 quantization, softmax, and RMSNorm training kernels for forward and backward passes.\nL209: \nL210: ### LM-head & Loss\nL211: \nL212: Sub-issue: cite84†#6599 L213: \nL214: Chunked LM-head with fused cross-entropy or policy loss, including memory-bounded backward for training.\nL215: ### Sampling\nL216: \nL217: Sub-issue: cite85†#6600 L218: \nL219: Fused radix top-k/top-p sampling, architecture qualification, kernel and dispatch optimizations, source/loader refactoring, and CUDA graph replay tests.\nL220: \nL221: ### Vision Encoder\nL222: \nL223: Sub-issue: cite86†#6601 L224: \nL225: Kimi-K3 vision tower kernels for MoonViT-3D and PatchMergerV2.\nL226: \nL227: ### Cross-family Support\nL228: \nL229: Sub-issue: cite87†#6602 L230: \nL231: Rubin/SM107 support and tuning across GDN, KDA, routing, BGMV MoE and MLA K concatenation; MiniMax-H3 SM120 shared kernels/helpers.\nL232: ### Standalone Build of CAKE Packages\nL233: \nL234: Sub-issue: cite88†#6553 L235: \nL236: The seven CAKE packages (`cake_rmsnorm_train`, `cake_dsa_train`, `cake_dsa_indexer`, `cake_lm_head_loss`, `dense_projection_gemm`, `cake_moe_grouped_gemm`, `cake_mok_bf16`) build and test outside flashinfer without patches: `build.json` manifests and a shared loader, header-free bindings, behaviour switches as keyword arguments, and backend test suites that import only the package.\nL237:   * cite89†refactor(cake): self-contained CAKE package directories behind thin core facades (#6553 step 1) #6571 L238:   * cite90†refactor(cake): build.json manifests, shared cake_build loader, header-free bindings; MoK sm_107a BF16/MXFP8 kernels (#6553 steps 2-4) #6584 L239:   * cite91†refactor(cake): behavior switches as keyword arguments; backend tests import only the package (#6553 asks 8, 9) #6610 L240: \nL241: Reactions are currently unavailable\nL242: ## Activity\nL243: \nL244: cite92†Next L245: \nL246:   1. cite75†yyihuang L247: \nL248: self-assigned this\nL249: \nL250: cite93†on Jul 29, 2026 L251: \nL252:   2. cite75†yyihuang L253: \nL254: added the\nL255: \nL256: cite70†Task L257: \nL258: issue type cite94†on Jul 29, 2026 L259: \nL260:   3. cite95†github-actions L261: \nL262: added\nL263: \nL264: cite72†needs-triage L265: \nL266: cite96†on Jul 29, 2026 L267: \nL268:   4. cite97†yzh119 L269: \nL270: changed the title ~~[-][CAKE] Long-term Blackwell Kernel Export Effort Tracker[/-]~~ [+][CAKE] Long-term CAKE-generated Kernel Progress Tracker[/+] cite98†on Jul 30, 2026 L271: \nL272:   5. cite75†yyihuang L273: \nL274: assigned\nL275: \nL276: cite97†yzh119 L277: \nL278: and\nL279: \nL280: cite99†xslingcn L281: \nL282: cite100†on Jul 30, 2026 L283:   6. cite75†yyihuang L284: \nL285: added 6 commits that reference this issue cite101†on Aug 3, 2026 L286: \nL287: cite102†feat(cake_kda): add optimized B200 recurrent prefill backend ( cite103†#4262 )\nL288: \nL289: ...\nL290: \nL291: cite102†1d2fc15 L292: \nL293: cite104†feat(cake_kda): add optimized B200 recurrent decode backend ( cite105†#4279 )\nL294: \nL295: ...\nL296: \nL297: cite104†4433996 L298: \nL299: cite106†feat(cake_kda): share recurrent prefill kernels across SM100 family ( cite107†#… L300: \nL301: ...\nL302: \nL303: cite106†d7e390c L304: \nL305: cite108†feat(cake_kda): share recurrent decode kernels across SM100 family ( cite109†#… L306: \nL307: ...\nL308: \nL309: cite108†968fa04 L310: cite110†feat(cake_tinygemm2): add CAKE-generated SM100/SM103 tinygemm2 varian… L311: \nL312: ...\nL313: \nL314: cite110†339a8f4 L315: \nL316: cite111†fix(cake_kda): support non-aligned recurrent prefill head counts ( cite112†#4351 )\nL317: \nL318: ...\nL319: \nL320: cite111†38bf507 L321: \nL322:   7. cite113†bkryu L323: \nL324: added a commit that references this issue cite114†on Aug 11, 2026 L325: \nL326: cite115†perf(cake_tinygemm2): add a STAGES=16 kernel tier for single-wave lar… L327: \nL328: ...\nL329: \nL330: cite115†78e463b L331: \nL332:   8. ### Kim2026-dev commented on Aug 14, 2026\nL333: \nL334: cite116†Kim2026-dev L335: \nL336: cite117†on Aug 14, 2026 L337: \nL338: More actions\nL339: # CAKE kernel candidates for MiniMax-H3 on B300 and RTX 5090\nL340: \nL341: Thank you for inviting customized kernel challenges in the CAKE tracker. We have\nL342: a MiniMax-H3 FL2VA runtime based on Sol Engine and SGLang and would like to ask\nL343: whether any of the standalone kernels below would be useful CAKE challenges.\nL344: These are independent candidates rather than a request for the CAKE team to\nL345: implement all of them. We will take care of Sol Engine/SGLang integration,\nL346: collectives, quantized checkpoints, calibration, end-to-end validation, and\nL347: deployment.\nL348: \nL349: The two targets are:\nL350: \nL351:      * NVIDIA B300 / SM103a, with Ulysses SP1/SP2/SP4/SP8;\nL352:      * NVIDIA RTX 5090 / SM120, quantized execution and SP1 only.\nL353: ## B300 / SM103a candidates\nL354: \nL355: Common H3 dimensions:\nL356: \nL357:      * hidden size: 5,376\nL358:      * heads: 56\nL359:      * head dimension: 128\nL360:      * attention inner dimension: 7,168\nL361:      * FFN dimension: 14,336\nL362:      * supported Ulysses degree `P`: 1, 2, 4, or 8\nL363:      * heads per rank after all-to-all: `56 / P` = 56, 28, 14, or 7\nL364:      * non-causal packed-varlen attention\nL365:      * batch size: 1\nL366: \nL367: For B300, we are interested in separate shape specializations for SP1, SP2,\nL368: SP4, and SP8.\nL369: Nominal `M` values for our main 768p duration buckets are:\nL370: \nL371: Duration  | Global packed rows `T`  | SP1 `M`  | SP2 `M`  | SP4 `M`  | SP8 `M`\nL372: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL373: 4 s  | 33,472  | 33,472  | 16,736  | 8,368  | 4,184\nL374: 5 s  | 38,592  | 38,592  | 19,296  | 9,648  | 4,824\nL375: 6 s  | 48,768  | 48,768  | 24,384  | 12,192  | 6,096\nL376: 8 s  | 58,944  | 58,944  | 29,472  | 14,736  | 7,368\nL377: 10 s  | 74,240  | 74,240  | 37,120  | 18,560  | 9,280\nL378: 15 s  | 109,952  | 109,952  | 54,976  | 27,488  | 13,744\nL379: Prompt length makes `M` slightly dynamic, so kernels need tail handling around\nL380: these values. We can provide exact tensor traces and a PyTorch reference for each\nL381: operator below.\nL382: ## 1. Fused BF16 pre-attention kernel — highest priority\nL383: \nL384: Reference operation:\nL385: \nL386:     `x [M, 5376]\nL387:       -> RMSNorm\nL388:       -> indexed AdaLN scale/shift\nL389:       -> BF16 QKV GEMM [M, 5376] x [5376, 21504]\nL390:       -> Q/K RMSNorm over D=128\nL391:       -> 3-D RoPE on Q/K\nL392:       -> destination-major BF16 QKV\nL393:            [P, M, 56/P, 3, 128]\nL394:     `\nL395: The output is only a send buffer; NCCL all-to-all is outside the kernel. The goal\nL396: is to avoid writing normalized x, modulated x, ordinary QKV, normalized Q/K, and\nL397: RoPE Q/K to HBM. `P` may be implemented as four compile-time specializations\nL398: instead of one dynamic kernel if that produces better code.\nL399: ## 2. Fused low-precision pre-attention kernels\nL400: \nL401: Same operation and output layout as kernel 1, with two independent variants:\nL402: \nL403:     `A. MXFP8/FP8 QKV GEMM\nL404:        -> BF16 Q/K RMSNorm + RoPE\nL405:        -> destination-major E4M3 QKV + scales\nL406: \nL407:     B. NVFP4 W4A4 QKV GEMM\nL408:        -> BF16 Q/K RMSNorm + RoPE\nL409:        -> destination-major NVFP4 QKV + block scales\nL410:     `\nL411: \nL412: An additional NVFP4-GEMM-to-E4M3-output variant is useful if the matching NVFP4\nL413: attention kernel is not accurate enough.\nL414: We will provide prepacked weights and scale tensors. The kernel does not need to\nL415: create or calibrate quantized weights.\nL416: ## 3. Packed-varlen FlashAttention-4 kernels\nL417: \nL418: Input after our existing Ulysses all-to-all:\nL419: \nL420:     `Q/K/V: [T, 56/P, 128]\nL421:     cu_seqlens: int32\nL422:     causal: false\nL423:     output: BF16 [T, 56/P, 128]\nL424:     `\nL425: \nL426: Nominal `T` centers are 33,472, 38,592, 48,768, 58,944, 74,240, and\nL427: 109,952. Requested standalone variants:\nL428: \nL429:     `A. BF16 FA4\nL430:     B. E4M3 FP8 FA4 with explicit descales\nL431:     C. experimental block-scaled NVFP4 FA4\nL432:     `\nL433: For C, we would be interested in a genuine low-precision Tensor Core implementation\nL434: rather than NVFP4 storage followed by BF16 matmuls. Softmax remains FP32. It would\nL435: be helpful to report the actual QK and PV MMA dtypes separately; a hybrid\nL436: NVFP4-QK / FP8-or-BF16-PV candidate would also be useful.\nL437: ## 4. Direct-layout attention output projection\nL438: \nL439: Reference operation:\nL440: \nL441:     `inverse-Ulysses receive layout [P, M, 56/P, 128]\nL442:       -> read without a standalone unpack/transpose\nL443:       -> O GEMM [M, 7168] x [7168, 5376]\nL444:       -> indexed gate * output + residual\nL445:       -> BF16 [M, 5376]\nL446:     `\nL447: \nL448: Requested GEMM variants: BF16, MXFP8/FP8, and NVFP4 W4A4. The collective itself\nL449: is outside the kernel.\nL450: ## 5. Fused RMSNorm + AdaLN + FC1 + SwiGLU\nL451: \nL452: Reference operation:\nL453: \nL454:     `x [M, 5376]\nL455:       -> RMSNorm\nL456:       -> indexed AdaLN scale/shift\nL457:       -> FC1 [M, 5376] x [5376, 28672]\nL458:       -> split gate/up\nL459:       -> SiLU(gate) * up\nL460:       -> BF16 [M, 14336]\nL461:     `\nL462: \nL463: Requested GEMM variants: BF16, MXFP8/FP8, and NVFP4 W4A4.\nL464: ## 6. Persistent full MLP candidate\nL465: \nL466: Reference operation:\nL467: \nL468:     `RMSNorm + indexed AdaLN\nL469:       -> FC1 [M, 5376] x [5376, 28672]\nL470:       -> SwiGLU\nL471:       -> FC2 [M, 14336] x [14336, 5376]\nL472:       -> indexed gate * output + residual\nL473:       -> BF16 [M, 5376]\nL474:     `\nL475: \nL476: Requested variants: BF16, MXFP8/FP8, and NVFP4 W4A4. This is only worth keeping\nL477: if it beats kernel 5 plus a tuned standalone FC2 GEMM; CAKE does not need to solve\nL478: that scheduling decision outside the kernel benchmark.\nL479: ## 7. Quantize-and-pack helper kernels\nL480: \nL481: These are useful fallbacks when the GEMM epilogue cannot write the communication\nL482: layout directly:\nL483: \nL484:     `BF16 Q/K/V [M, 56, 128]\nL485:       -> destination-major E4M3 + scales [P, M, 56/P, 3, 128]\nL486: \nL487:     BF16 Q/K/V [M, 56, 128]\nL488:       -> destination-major NVFP4 + block scales [P, M, 56/P, 3, 128]\nL489:     `\nL490: \nL491: Quantization and relayout should happen in one HBM pass.\nL492: ## RTX 5090 / SM120 quantized SP1 candidates\nL493: \nL494: If CAKE currently supports SM120, we would also appreciate considering a smaller\nL495: set of single-GPU kernels for the quantized H3 FL2VA path on RTX 5090. This target\nL496: uses SP1 only, so there is no Ulysses layout or collective in these kernels.\nL497: \nL498: For SP1, `M = T`; the nominal M values are 33,472, 38,592, 48,768, 58,944,\nL499: 74,240, and 109,952 for 4/5/6/8/10/15 seconds. We are interested in two quantized\nL500: GEMM formats:\nL501:      * W8A8 E4M3 FP8;\nL502:      * NVIDIA-compatible block-scaled NVFP4 W4A4.\nL503: \nL504: BF16 is used as the numerical reference but does not need a separately tuned 5090\nL505: kernel in this request.\nL506: ### 5090-K1. Quantized fused pre-attention\nL507: \nL508:     `x [M, 5376]\nL509:       -> RMSNorm + indexed AdaLN\nL510:       -> FP8 or NVFP4 QKV GEMM [M, 5376] x [5376, 21504]\nL511:       -> BF16 Q/K RMSNorm + 3-D RoPE\nL512:       -> Q/K/V [M, 56, 128]\nL513:     `\nL514: \nL515: Useful output variants would be BF16, E4M3 plus scales, and NVFP4 plus block\nL516: scales, so that we can connect the best one to the corresponding attention path.\nL517: ### 5090-K2. Quantized packed-varlen FA4\nL518: \nL519:     `Q/K/V [T, 56, 128]\nL520:     cu_seqlens: int32\nL521:     causal: false\nL522:     output: BF16 [T, 56, 128]\nL523:     `\nL524: \nL525: The requested candidates are E4M3 FP8 FA4 and experimental block-scaled NVFP4\nL526: FA4. Softmax should remain FP32. For the NVFP4 candidate, it would be helpful to\nL527: report the QK and PV MMA dtypes separately and include a hybrid NVFP4-QK /\nL528: FP8-or-BF16-PV result if it is more accurate or faster.\nL529: ### 5090-K3. Quantized attention output projection\nL530: \nL531:     `attention output [M, 7168]\nL532:       -> FP8 or NVFP4 O GEMM [M, 7168] x [7168, 5376]\nL533:       -> indexed gate * output + residual\nL534:       -> BF16 [M, 5376]\nL535:     `\nL536: \nL537: ### 5090-K4. Quantized FC1 + SwiGLU\nL538: \nL539:     `x [M, 5376]\nL540:       -> RMSNorm + indexed AdaLN\nL541:       -> FP8 or NVFP4 FC1 [M, 5376] x [5376, 28672]\nL542:       -> SwiGLU\nL543:       -> BF16 [M, 14336]\nL544:     `\nL545: ### 5090-K5. Quantized persistent full MLP candidate\nL546: \nL547:     `RMSNorm + indexed AdaLN\nL548:       -> FP8 or NVFP4 FC1\nL549:       -> SwiGLU\nL550:       -> FP8 or NVFP4 FC2 [M, 14336] x [14336, 5376]\nL551:       -> indexed gate * output + residual\nL552:       -> BF16 [M, 5376]\nL553:     `\nL554: As with the B300 candidates, this full MLP would only be useful if it outperforms\nL555: the fused FC1 + SwiGLU kernel followed by a tuned standalone FC2 kernel. We will\nL556: provide prepacked quantized weights and scales; weight conversion and calibration\nL557: are not part of the kernel request.\nL558: \nL559: For RTX 5090, our preferred starting point would be 5090-K4 NVFP4 FC1 +\nL560: SwiGLU, followed by 5090-K1 and the FP8/NVFP4 attention candidates.\nL561: ## Integration\nL562: \nL563: For any selected candidate, a FlashInfer-compatible kernel implementation and\nL564: basic benchmark results would be very helpful. We will handle the Sol\nL565: Engine/SGLang integration and end-to-end evaluation.\nL566: \nL567: 👍React with 👍1 Reacted by eigen\nL568: \nL569: 👀React with 👀1 Reacted by eigen\nL570: \nL571:   9. cite75†yyihuang L572: \nL573: added a sub-issue cite118†on Aug 15, 2026 L574: \nL575:      * cite119†CAKE kernel candidates for MiniMax-H3 on B300 and RTX 5090 #4532 L576: \nL577:   10. ### 203 remaining items\nL578: \nL579: Load more\nL580: \nL581: Load more actions\nL582: \nL583:   11. cite75†yyihuang L584: added sub-issues cite120†on Oct 16, 2026 L585: \nL586:      * cite79†[CAKE] Attention Kernel Progress Tracker #6594 L587: \nL588:      * cite80†[CAKE] Linear Attention & State Space Kernel Progress Tracker #6595 L589: \nL590:      * cite81†[CAKE] GEMM / BMM Kernel Progress Tracker #6596 L591: \nL592:      * cite82†[CAKE] MoE & Routing Kernel Progress Tracker #6597 L593: \nL594:      * cite83†[CAKE] Activation & Quantization Kernel Progress Tracker #6598 L595: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nForgeStencil: Automating Per-Case Stencil Specialization from Kernels to 100+ Real Applications (https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06694v2)\nciteturn18view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06694v2\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 489\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRelease Atrex Kernel Agent v0.3.0 — Long-horizon optimization and production campaigns · alibaba/atrex-kernel-agent · GitHub (https://github.com/alibaba/atrex-kernel-agent/releases/tag/v0.3.0)\nciteturn18view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/alibaba/atrex-kernel-agent/releases/tag/v0.3.0\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 199\n-------------------------------------------------